      "notes": "Verdict is well-scoped. The 'measurable' tier label on the E11 claim is slightly generous \u2014 E11 is from eff.org (advocacy/media) and uses 'could exclude millions', which is a projection not a measured baseline. This is a warning-level concern but not blocking given the claim itself uses conditional language ('could exclude') and the verdict's overall direction is negligible with low confidence. All three claims are supported by their quoted evidence. No tier confusion in the direction/magnitude/time_horizon combination (negligible direction with minor magnitude is an edge case but acceptable here as the rationale explains the 'soft-verb' logic). No party-blind issues, no false balance, no lever leakage."
